      "count": 4,
      "label": "Upper-Division Psychology Electives",
      "notes": "Select four additional elective courses (16 units) from Psychology 101 to 188 or 199B. Courses must be taken for a minimum of 4 units and for a letter grade. Psychology 134A through 134E, 184A, 184B, and 188SA through 188SC, along with all laboratory courses (Psychology 101, 111, M116A, 116B, 121, 126, 131, 136A, 136B, M136C, 151, 158, and 186A through 186F) may not be applied. Students who complete Psychology M117A, M117B, and M117C may receive equivalent credit for course 115 under Category A and two upper-division psychology electives. All three courses must be completed to receive any psychology elective credit."
     }
